<urn:atm:triage:finding/AX3-QA5-004>
  a triage:Finding ;
  triage:findingId "AX3-QA5-004" ;
  triage:title "Sprint AX.3 doc has no traceability for the ReaderPool drop/join lifecycle change landed on its branch; the component belongs to the already-merged Phase AV (AV.1a) and the sprint doc does not record the fix as an AX.3 deliverable or out-of-scope carry" ;
  triage:description "AX.3 QA-5 (quality-mgr ax3-qa-r5, PR #1191 Final Quality Report 2026-09-05T11:07Z; req-qa ATM-QA-AX3R-003, confirmed by quality-mgr) at head c6525fd11. The AX3-QA4-001 fix changes crates/atm-storage-rusqlite/src/reader_pool.rs (ReaderPool shutdown/join on last-owner drop), a component owned by Phase AV sprint AV.1a, but docs/plans/phase-ax/sprint-AX.3-task-state-machine.md contains no mention of ReaderPool, reader lanes, or the drop/join lifecycle, so a reader of the AX.3 sprint doc cannot trace why the change is on this branch. Fix: add a short 'Carried fixes outside sprint scope' (or equivalent) note to the AX.3 sprint doc naming AX3-QA3-001/AX3-QA4-001, the reader_pool.rs Drop/join change, its AV.1a origin, and the tests that prove it. HEAD confirmed via git grep -n -i -E 'ReaderPool|reader pool|reader_pool' HEAD -- docs/plans/phase-ax/sprint-AX.3-task-state-machine.md: no match (exit code 1), confirming the sprint doc has zero ReaderPool traceability at c6525fd1168da1080ad4aa02e253d833b32c4fe9. Occurrence is anchored on the doc's Deliverables section heading (line 129) as the expected-but-missing location for the carry-forward note. References: PR #1191 comment https://github.com/randlee/atm-core/pull/1191#issuecomment-5551352363; prior triage record .triage/phase-ax/findings/AX3-QA4-001.ttl (records the underlying AX3-QA4-001 reader_pool.rs Drop/join fix this doc gap fails to trace)." ;
